(* fs-registration R4, documented limitation, K_reg = 1 (expected FALSE):
   two Server objects built from the same identity key have separate
   consumed sets, so both accept the bundle of one honest Beacon (the
   FsBeaconStarted premise selects honest bundles).  This is the expected
   consequence of owner decision OD2: replay claims are per live Server
   state, and R1 and R1' are stated per object. *)
query s: bitstring, s2: bitstring, b: bitstring, init: beaconcrypt_core__pqxdh__t_VerifiedInitKex,
      o1: bitstring, o2: bitstring, i1: beaconcrypt_core__pqxdh__t_VerifiedInitKex, i2: beaconcrypt_core__pqxdh__t_VerifiedInitKex, rid: beaconcrypt_core__pqxdh__t_RegistrationId,
      r1: bitstring, r2: bitstring, i: time, j: time;
  event(FsBeaconStarted(s2, b, init, rid))
  && event(FsServerAccepted(o1, s, b, i1, rid, r1))@i
  && event(FsServerAccepted(o2, s, b, i2, rid, r2))@j
  ==> i = j.

process FsRegistrationMain()
